%S A399142 1,0,1,0,1,4,0,1,21,36,0,1,102,552,576,0,1,535,6990,19560,14400,0,1,
%T A399142 3098,89250,504720,920160,518400,0,1,19691,1211084,12395250,42038640,
%U A399142 55974240,25401600,0,1,136062,17730412,310725800,1747569600,4127114880,4293596160,1625702400
%N A399142 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) counts trees on [n] rooted at 1 together with a level assignment L:[n]->{0,...,k} that uses every level, has L(1)=0, and strictly increases from parent to child, 0<=k<=n-1.
%C A399142 An edge may skip levels: if u is the parent of v, only L(u)<L(v) is required, not L(v)=L(u)+1. Thus the levels need not equal distances from the root. For k=0, T(1,0)=1 counts the one-vertex tree with its unique level assignment, while T(n,0)=0 for n>=2 because a nontrivial tree has an edge but only level 0 is available.
%F A399142 Let f(x)=x*exp(x), and let f^t(x) denote its formal t-th iterate under composition. f^t(x) = Sum_{n>=1} x^n/(n-1)! * Sum_{k=0..n-1} binomial(t,k) * T(n,k).
%F A399142 T(n,0) = delta(n,1); T(n,k) = Sum_{j=k..n-1} j^(n-j) * binomial(n-1,j-1) * T(j,k-1) for n>=2 and 1<=k<=n-1.
%F A399142 T(n,2) = A080108(n) - 2 = A185298(n)/n - 2 for n>=3.
%F A399142 T(n,n-1) = A001044(n-1).
%F A399142 T(n+1,n-1) = A292062(n).
%F A399142 Sum_{k=0..n-1} (-1)^(n-1-k) * T(n,k) = A000272(n).
%e A399142 T(3,2)=4. If L(2)=1 and L(3)=2, then vertex 2 must have parent 1, while vertex 3 may have parent 1 or 2, giving two pairs. Interchanging vertices 2 and 3 gives two more. The star centered at the root is counted twice, once for each level assignment.
%e A399142 Triangle begins:
%e A399142   n\k| 0  1      2        3         4         5         6         7
%e A399142   ---+--------------------------------------------------------------
%e A399142    1 | 1;
%e A399142    2 | 0, 1;
%e A399142    3 | 0, 1,     4;
%e A399142    4 | 0, 1,    21,      36;
%e A399142    5 | 0, 1,   102,     552,      576;
%e A399142    6 | 0, 1,   535,    6990,    19560,    14400;
%e A399142    7 | 0, 1,  3098,   89250,   504720,   920160,   518400;
%e A399142    8 | 0, 1, 19691, 1211084, 12395250, 42038640, 55974240, 25401600;
%p A399142 T:= proc(n,k) option remember; `if`(k=0, `if`(n=1, 1, 0),
%p A399142       add(j^(n-j)*binomial(n-1, j-1)*T(j, k-1), j=k..n-1))
%p A399142     end:
%p A399142 seq(seq(T(n, k), k=0..n-1), n=1..9);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Aug 20 2026
%o A399142 (PARI) T(n, k) = if(k==0, n==1, sum(j=k, n-1, j^(n-j)*binomial(n-1, j-1)*T(j, k-1)));
%Y A399142 Diagonals give A001044, A292062.
%Y A399142 Cf. A008826, A154372, A185298, A080108, A000272.
%K A399142 nonn,tabl,new
%O A399142 1,6
